  == page 14 ==
Saint Lucia Population and Housing Census - 2022
Considering that 94% of households are domestic electricity consumers (Table 19), it would be
reasonable to validate the household data in Table 1, using the number of LUCELEC’s domestic
consumer accounts for accuracy. Since the number of domestic consumers rose from 53,566 in
December 2010 to 63,222 in 2021, and 63,849 by the end of 2022 given that 94.1% of households use
electricity for domestic consumption (Table B.5). An interpolation of LUCELEC data of 63,350
domestic consumers, while maintaining a 94.1% rate for all private households, results in an estimate
of 67,322 households. Given that some households have multiple electricity accounts, the resultant
estimate closely matches the number of households in Table 1 and validates the housing data for
Census 2022.
International research on census undercounts is ongoing, in many countries, this phenomenon has been
discussed in the 2020 Round of Censuses and is important in the Eastern Caribbean Region. Research
could give rise to improved methods of estimating the undercount and could eventually lead to a
revision of the provisional numbers of the census report (census undercount ).
Population Size
Saint Lucia recorded an overall household population increase of 3.8% (Table A.1) on 12/13 March
2022, this increase was based on a point-to-point calculation of the two censuses. At midnight on
Census Night, 12/13 March 2022, the total resident population stood at 172,948 people. The total
population including visiting non-resident people was estimated to be 178,807, the reported number
of non-resident visitors was 5,859. Out of the resident population, 1,114 individuals live in institutions,
while the household residents comprise 171,834 people. (Table 3), made up of 84,716 males and
87,119 females (Tables A.1 and A.3). Among the ten enumeration districts, household population
declines were observed in Castries, Anse La Raye, and Soufriere, with Castries experiencing the largest
decrease (Table A.2).
